<section class="work-chapter section" id="organizations"><div class="container work-grid"><div class="work-intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Advisory</p><h2>Make the organization easier to understand, manage and trust.</h2><p>An organization is a set of decisions, responsibilities, habits and relationships that must work together under pressure. Useful advisory work begins where that coordination breaks down.</p><a class="arrow-link" href="<%= site.externalLinks.jkmns %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Learn about JKMNS <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="small-note">JKMNS is a separate professional firm. This page describes experience and intellectual interests, not a direct services contract.</p></div><ol class="focus-list"><% page.data.organizations.forEach((item, i) => { %><li><span>0<%= i+1 %></span><div><h3><%= item[0] %></h3><p><%= item[1] %></p></div></li><% }) %></ol></div></section>
<section class="work-chapter section section-teal" id="education"><div class="container work-grid"><div class="work-intro"><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">02 / Academia</p><h2>Teaching is not the transfer of a finished answer.</h2><p>In management and finance, the most interesting problems often involve incomplete information or competing objectives. Theory matters; so does knowing when it applies, where it falls short and what responsibility looks like in practice.</p><a class="arrow-link arrow-light" href="<%= urlFor('/insights/research/') %>">View selected research <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><ol class="focus-list"><% page.data.education.forEach((item, i) => { %><li><span>0<%= i+1 %></span><div><h3><%= item[0] %></h3><p><%= item[1] %></p></div></li><% }) %></ol></div></section>
<section class="work-chapter section" id="mentorship"><div class="container work-grid"><div class="work-intro"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Mentorship</p><h2>Do not build a young person's future for them. Help them learn to build it.</h2><p>The most useful contribution is often helping someone become more capable of making an independent decision.</p><p class="small-note">Guidance and mentoring do not guarantee admissions, scholarships or employment outcomes.</p></div><div class="theme-stack"><% page.data.mentoringThemes.forEach((item) => { %><span><%= item %></span><% }) %></div></div></section>
<section class="section progress-note"><div class="container split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">How I think about progress</p><h2>Start with the problem, not the presentation.</h2></div><div class="prose-large"><p>Before recommending a solution, I want to know what is actually happening, what evidence is available, who lives with the consequences and what success would look like after the project ends.</p><p>The same principle applies in a classroom. A polished answer is not enough if the learner cannot explain how they reached it.</p></div></div></section>
